    "description": "Ribomic Inc. engages in the discovery and development of pharmaceutical compounds using RNA aptamers in Japan and Europe. The company develops RBM-007, which is in Phase III clinical trial for the treatment of achondroplasia; Phase II clinical trial for the treatment of wet age-related macular degeneration; and pre-clinical trial for the treatment of diabetic macular edema. It is also involved in the development of drugs in pre-clinical trial stage, including RBM-006 for the treatment of retinal disease, proliferative, vitreoretinopathy, glaucoma, and diabetic retinopathy; RBM-011 for the treatment of pulmonary arterial hypertension; RBM-003 for the treatment of heart failure; RBM-010 for the treatment of osteoarthritis; and RBM-009 for the treatment of severe asthma, as well as RBM-101, which is in discovery stage for the affinity purification of human IgG and Fc-fusion proteins. The company was incorporated in 2003 and is headquartered in Minato, Japan."
